/* ============================================================================
median-of-data.epher -- the middle of a dataset, even and odd counts

The median of ten exam scores (an even count: the mean of the two middle
values) and of a five-score set (an odd count: the middle value itself),
from the builtin median (guide 1.20) and by hand on the sorted list.

Run it from a terminal:
  Linux (deb, rpm):  epher /usr/lib/epher/scripts/statistics/summary/median-of-data.epher
  Windows:           epher "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\epher\scripts\statistics\summary\median-of-data.epher"
  macOS:             epher /Applications/epher.app/Contents/Resources/scripts/statistics/summary/median-of-data.epher
In the REPL:             load one of the paths above
Web/desktop:             paste the whole file into the entry, press Enter
Everything also works line by line in the TUI.

The one knob to edit is `d` below. Everything above the results section
is machinery you can leave alone.
============================================================================ */

// ---- the knobs -----------------------------------------------------------------
const d = {72, 85, 91, 64, 88, 79, 83, 95, 70, 86}   // exam scores, 10 students (even count)
const od = {64, 70, 72, 79, 83}                      // a five-score set (odd count)

// ---- median of the even count: the mean of the two middle values ---------------
median(d)                   // builtin median
s = sort(d)                 // the sorted list; the two middle entries straddle
(s[5] + s[6]) / 2           // the 5th and 6th sorted scores, averaged by hand

// ---- median of the odd count: the middle value itself ---------------------------
median(od)                  // builtin median of the five scores

/* ---- expected output ----
= {72, 85, 91, 64, 88, 79, 83, 95, 70, 86}
= {64, 70, 72, 79, 83}
= 84
= {64, 70, 72, 79, 83, 85, 86, 88, 91, 95}
= 84
= 72
*/